**G2 — fence parser blind classes for `piMaterializeMismatch`.** Two gaps: (i) template-first-arg — `inject-compartments-pi.ts:1296-1297` mints `piMaterializeMismatch(\`render_config:mural(...)\`, …)`, bridged only because TS independently mints `render_config:*` into the stem arm; a NEW Pi-side composite via this path reaches receipts outside doc↔code equality. I extended the stem-arm scan to `piMaterializeMismatch\(\s*\`([a-z_]+)(?::|[(:])`. (ii) variable-first-arg — applied the same unmapped-variable law already enforced on the `reason:` surface (producers.test.ts:399-403) to mismatch mints; a variable first arg not in the explicit map reddens. Controls: in-memory plant of a fake template composite + a fake variable mint → both reddened; asserted the live mural template at :1296 is now parser-visible (named it in the fence/doc set so its coverage is explicit, verified the token appears in the doc fence). Added a doc coverage sentence.

**G3 — zone floors.** Every `existsSync`-filtered walk can silently zero a zone: rust-parity test `RUST_PROD_ROOTS` (mc-store + mc-tokenizer have no floor; only the two planted crates do), `system-region-clear.test.ts` `RUST_ROOTS`/`TS_ROOTS` walk (:361-369 continues on missing dir). Added: (a) expected-zone assertion — the four crates under `crates/` (canonical set) must all be present-and-walked, missing = law fails with the zone named; (b) `walkedFiles` floor per zone (&gt;0 with the count recorded in the failure message). I hit a bug in my own floor: iterating the passed list makes a dropped zone invisible — fixed to canonical-membership (check membership in the canonical set, not presence in the walked list). Applied to both the rust-parity test and the clear-file census.

