## 504-536 · Storm defect dispatch received; source verification and Fix B adjudication begun
The coordinator dispatched a consolidated fix round (baseline `c15ddeb48`) with two parts: Part 1 — a field-verified storm defect plus its fix and laws; Part 2 — round-3 residuals H1–H4 (intra-blessed-file blindness, fold-body reason parser asymmetry, Pi refusal census zone hole, walk extension/dot-dir blind). One end-of-turn report, no mid-run coordinator messages, full batteries once at the end (production code changes this time).

**Storm defect root cause (confirmed at source by me):** The rotation comparator compares two structurally different sources. The captured side uses the real persisted content hash (`snapshotMarkersFromCachedM0` → `cached_m0_project_docs_hash`), but the current side (`readCurrentM0SnapshotMarkers`) hardcodes `projectDocsHash: ""` — legitimately for the head lane (the HARD renderer replaces it before persist), but the region promotion feeds it raw into `DELTA_TRIGGER_FIELDS` which includes `projectDocsHash`. Result: every boundary-permission pass in a tool-loop marathon rotated with `reason=project_docs_hash`, `executed=true`, identical 63,556 bytes, forever; column==live hash yet perpetual stale. FPE involvement refuted (fpe.ts is stateless). Filesystem/mtime fingerprint churn refuted (fingerprint is pure cache key; comparator's current side never touches fs). Provider cache stayed warm because re-rendered bytes were identical — but each rotation set `bustedThisPass=true`, which drove 140× `dropSlot("lkg_refresh_declined")` + 493× capture declines `build_no_anchor`: `findLkgAnchor` structurally refuses to capture mid-tool-loop (active assistant requires a real user strictly after it, `lkg-replay.ts:256-285`), and `transform.ts` `bustedThisPass &amp;&amp; !captured → dropSlot`. One event (the fake bust) invalidated the durable slot AND blocked re-establishment — L0 violation at the slot level.

**Pi mirror defect (discovered during my source verification):** Pi's wrapper has the mirror defect — the persisted value appears on both sides of the comparison, so the trigger can never fire. This means Pi's rotation comparator is structurally dead (never promotes), unlike TS which perpetually promotes.

I read the wiring law file (`system-region-wiring.test.ts`) that hid the defect for 11 rounds — its `live({})` shape equal to captured was the blind spot. The anti-vacuity law requirement from the dispatch: the warm-boundary-never-promotes law must derive `currentMarkers` via the production reader composition (a shared helper both law and wiring use), never a hand-shaped fixture.

**Fix B adjudication (in progress at chunk boundary):** I began enumerating every durable-LKG-row consumer to answer the coordinator's open question: does any LKG replay consumer use the durable row UNCONDITIONALLY (serve without validating the slot corresponds to current derived state), or is replay gated on freshness/identity? I read `lkg-replay.ts`, the `transform.ts` drop chain, checked build-refusal reasons, and examined the Pi mirror of the drop chain. The ruling determines whether to keep the durable row on no_anchor/missing_ids-class build refusals (gated → keep + log `lkg_kept reason=no_reanchor`) or make capture survive the loop (unconditional → allow capture on mid-loop bust passes anchored at the turn's own leading user when served prefix hasn't diverged). H1–H4 not yet started.

